# Tally — Agent-era ActivityWatch

> **2026-05-02 — Emperor's directive.** ActivityWatch is great but (a) lacks a real GUI, (b) lacks cloud sync, (c) cannot be talked to by OpenClaw / PeopleClaw / any agent. This project rebuilds the AW experience for the agent era while preserving its excellent local backend.
>
> Configured via TDD-first methodology: **stories → tests → code**, never the other way around.

---

## 0. Vision

> Keep ActivityWatch's privacy-first local-first soul. Replace its 2014-era browser-based UI with a polished Electron desktop app. Add an opt-in, end-to-end-encrypted cloud sync so agents (OpenClaw, PeopleClaw, future) can answer questions like "what did Exis spend his day on?" without depending on a screen capture or a manual log.

### What we are NOT

| Not | Why |
|-----|-----|
| ❌ A reimplementation of `aw-server` | aw-server-rust already works, is tiny (~10 MB), and its REST API is stable. We embed it. |
| ❌ A SaaS-only tracker (Rize / RescueTime) | Privacy-first stays. Cloud sync is opt-in and E2EE. |
| ❌ A productivity-shaming dashboard | We surface raw events + agent-grade summaries. No "you wasted 3h on Reddit" UI. |
| ❌ Yet another pretty time chart | The deliverable for users IS a polished GUI; the deliverable for *agents* is the API. The chart is a side-effect. |

### What we ARE

> A native desktop app that supervises the AW backend, presents a beautiful local UI, and exposes the user's activity stream to the user's own AI agents — locally first, cloud-synced when permitted.

---

## 1. Architecture (Canonical, Source of Truth)

```
┌──────────────────────── Electron App (tally) ────────────────────────┐
│                                                                         │
│  ┌─ Renderer (React/Vite) ─────┐    ┌─ Main Process ───────────────┐  │
│  │  • Dashboard                │◄──►│  • Backend Supervisor (BE)   │  │
│  │  • Timeline                 │    │  • Tray + autostart          │  │
│  │  • Sync settings            │    │  • IPC bridge                │  │
│  │  • Agent token manager      │    │  • Cloud sync worker         │  │
│  └─────────────────────────────┘    └────────┬─────────────────────┘  │
│                                              │ spawns / supervises    │
│                                              ▼                         │
│                                  ┌─ Bundled subprocesses ─┐            │
│                                  │  aw-server-rust        │            │
│                                  │  aw-watcher-window     │            │
│                                  │  aw-watcher-afk        │            │
│                                  └────────────────────────┘            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                              │ HTTPS
                                              ▼
                ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                │  https://tally.rollersoft.com.au  (single domain)   │
                │  Next.js on Vercel + Turso (Drizzle) + Logto auth   │
                │                                                     │
                │   /                  → marketing landing            │
                │   /download          → installer downloads          │
                │   /app/*             → web dashboard (logged-in)    │
                │   /api/v1/sync/*     → desktop ⇄ cloud sync         │
                │   /api/v1/agent/*    → agent API (M2M)              │
                │   /api/internal/*    → e2e + cron, gated by secret  │
                └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                              │
                                              ▼
                              ┌──────────────────────────────┐
                              │  OpenClaw / PeopleClaw / etc │
                              │  (consumes via Agent API)    │
                              └──────────────────────────────┘
```

### 1.1 Component manifest

| # | Component | Tech | Lifecycle owner |
|---|-----------|------|-----------------|
| C1 | Electron Main | TypeScript, electron-builder | App |
| C2 | Renderer UI | React + Vite + DaisyUI | App |
| C3 | Backend Supervisor | Node child_process | Main process |
| C4 | Bundled `aw-server-rust` | upstream binary, vendored per-platform | Supervisor |
| C5 | Bundled watchers (`window`, `afk`) | upstream binaries | Supervisor |
| C6 | Local API wrapper | TypeScript SDK over `aw-server` REST | Renderer + Main |
| C7 | Cloud Sync Worker | Node, runs in Main, batches buckets | Main process |
| C8 | Cloud + Web (single Next.js app) | Next.js on Vercel + Turso (Drizzle) + Logto | Standalone monorepo sibling |
| C9 | Agent SDK | `@tally/agent` npm package | Standalone |

### 1.2 Repos / deploy targets

| Asset | Repo | Deploy |
|-------|------|--------|
| Electron app | `exisz/tally` (root: `apps/desktop`) | electron-builder → GitHub Releases |
| Cloud + Web (landing + dashboard + API) | same monorepo, root: `apps/cloud` (Next.js App Router) | **Single** Vercel project `tally`, **single** custom domain `tally.rollersoft.com.au` |
| Agent SDK | same monorepo, `packages/agent-sdk` | npm |

> **One project, one domain, one deploy.** The Next.js app at `apps/cloud` serves the landing page (`/`), the logged-in web dashboard (`/app`), the sync API (`/api/v1/sync`), and the agent API (`/api/v1/agent`). No separate landing project. No `aw.rollersoft.com.au` / `tally-landing` split.

### 1.3 Hard constraints

- ✅ **AW feature parity (non-negotiable)**: Tally MUST cover every user-facing feature of upstream ActivityWatch — see §1.4 Parity Matrix. New stories cannot replace AW features; they extend them.
- ✅ **Embedded backend**: never ask user to install ActivityWatch separately. Bundled `aw-server-rust` exposes its full REST API on loopback so 3rd-party AW watchers (vim, vscode, JetBrains, browser ext, obsidian, etc.) plug in unmodified.
- ✅ **Local-first**: app must be 100% functional with cloud sync OFF
- ✅ **E2EE for cloud**: events encrypted client-side with a key derived from a user-held passphrase; cloud sees only opaque blobs (except aggregate metadata needed for indexing — see §3)
- ✅ **Agent API**: agents authenticate via Logto M2M tokens scoped to a single user
- ✅ **TDD-first**: every story has a test under `tests/e2e/journeys/` or `tests/unit/` written **before** any production code
- ✅ **Cross-platform**: macOS (arm64 + x64), Windows (x64), Linux (x64) — match upstream AW

