## 2. Canonical User Scenarios (Source of Truth)

> These are **non-negotiable**. Any feature request that contradicts them must trigger an escalation, not silent reinterpretation.

| ID | Scenario | Acceptance |
|----|----------|------------|
| **S1** | Fresh install on a clean Mac → user double-clicks `.dmg` → drags to Applications → launches → tray icon appears → `aw-server` is running on a private port → window shows "0 events tracked (just started)" | E2E test `01-fresh-install.spec.ts` |
| **S2** | After 60 s of typing in VSCode and Chrome, the dashboard shows two distinct buckets with non-zero event counts; the timeline shows ≥1 colored block per app | `02-event-collection.spec.ts` |
| **S3** | User clicks "Enable cloud sync" → enters a passphrase → app generates an encryption key → uploads existing events in the background → cloud `GET /api/v1/sync/buckets` returns the user's bucket list (opaque ids only) | `03-cloud-sync-enable.spec.ts` |
| **S4** | An OpenClaw agent, holding an M2M token, calls `GET /api/v1/agent/summary?since=24h` and receives a structured JSON answer ("3 h 12 m on VSCode, 1 h 47 m on Chrome, 22 m AFK") — derived **client-side at decryption time** by a user-installed gateway, not from cloud plaintext | `05-agent-summary.spec.ts` |
| **S5** | User quits the Electron app → all spawned child processes (`aw-server`, watchers) terminate within 3 s; no orphans visible in `ps` | `06-clean-shutdown.spec.ts` |
| **S6** | User toggles "Pause tracking" in tray menu → no new events flow into any bucket until resumed | `07-pause-tracking.spec.ts` |
| **S7** | User revokes an agent token in cloud settings → next call by that agent returns 401 within 60 s | `08-agent-revocation.spec.ts` |
| **S8** | User uninstalls the app → all local data, child processes, autostart entries removed | `09-clean-uninstall.spec.ts` |

### 2.1 Anti-scenarios (will be rejected)

| Anti-pattern | Why rejected |
|--------------|--------------|
| ❌ Cloud receives plaintext window titles | Violates E2EE. |
| ❌ App requires an account to start tracking | Violates local-first. |
| ❌ App ships with productivity-shaming UI ("You're below your goal") | Out of scope; that's a separate agent's job. |
| ❌ Reimplementing `aw-server` in Node | Wastes effort; upstream Rust binary is excellent. |
| ❌ Auto-uploading without explicit opt-in | Privacy violation. |

---

## 3. Cloud Sync — E2EE design

| Layer | Visibility to cloud |
|-------|---------------------|
| Bucket id (UUID) | ✅ visible |
| Bucket type (e.g. `currentwindow`) | ✅ visible (needed for routing) |
| Event timestamp + duration | ✅ visible (needed for incremental sync) |
| Event `data` payload (app name, title, URL) | 🔒 **encrypted blob** (XChaCha20-Poly1305) |
| Per-user encryption key | ❌ never sent — derived from user passphrase via Argon2id |
| Per-device key share (multi-device unlock) | 🔒 wrapped with master, sent encrypted |

Cloud cannot read titles. Agent gateways decrypt locally on the user's behalf and serve summaries to OpenClaw etc.

---

## 4. TDD framework (Source of Truth for "how we build")

### 4.1 Layers

| Layer | Tool | Test root | Run cmd |
|-------|------|-----------|---------|
| Unit (pure logic) | **Vitest** | `tests/unit/` | `pnpm test:unit` |
| Integration (supervisor + bundled binaries) | **Vitest + child_process** | `tests/integration/` | `pnpm test:integration` |
| Electron E2E | **Playwright (electron driver)** | `tests/e2e/journeys/` | `pnpm test:e2e` |
| Cloud API E2E | **Playwright (HTTP)** | `apps/cloud/tests/e2e/` | `pnpm --filter cloud e2e` |

### 4.2 Story → Test rule (non-negotiable)

```
For every Story ticket (PLANET-XXXX):

  1. Acceptance criteria written in the ticket (Gherkin-ish)
  2. A failing test file exists at the path named in the ticket
  3. Test file is committed to main BEFORE any production code
  4. Engineer pod is gated on: "does the named test exist and currently fail?"
  5. Engineer marks Done only when test goes green AND test was not modified during implementation
```

### 4.3 Layout (mirrors peopleclaw)

```
apps/desktop/
  tests/
    e2e/
      fixtures/         # mock watchers, fake clock, tmp data dir
      helpers/          # spawn helpers, IPC helpers, waitFor
      journeys/         # 1 file per Canonical Scenario (S1..S8)
      pages/            # POMs (page object models) for renderer windows
    unit/
    integration/
  playwright.config.ts  # uses electron driver, headless, video on
apps/cloud/
  tests/
    e2e/                # mirrors peopleclaw apps/admin/tests/e2e
```

### 4.4 Reference implementation

The pattern is **identical** to PeopleClaw `apps/admin/tests/e2e/journeys/`. See:

- `peopleclaw/apps/admin/tests/e2e/journeys/08-scheduled-task.spec.ts` — for API-driven, fixture-minted-token style
- `peopleclaw/apps/admin/playwright.config.ts` — for `baseURL` env-overridable config

Differences for tally:

- Use `_electron` from `playwright` to launch the packaged app
- Use a **temporary `XDG_DATA_HOME` / `APPDATA`** per test for isolation
- Stub `aw-watcher-window` with a fake binary that emits scripted events on a deterministic clock

